Brandon's sock draw contains eight football socks ($F$) and ten workwear socks ($W$). Every morning he randomly selects two socks from the draw, without replacement.

The partial tree diagram below shows the outcomes and one probability.

\exfigure{718_q14_1}

parts.latex:
A partially completed tree diagram is shown.

\exfigure{850_q32_1}

Complete the tree diagram and find the probability that the ice cream machine is not working on at least one of the days when he visits.

solutions.latex:
\exfigure{850_q32_s1}

The machine not working on at least one day is the complement of it working on all three days.
$$\begin{aligned}P(\overline{W}\text{ on at least one day})&=1-P(WWW)\\&=1-(0.4)^3\\&=0.936\end{aligned}$$
